smoke rises over the northern Syrian  town of Rasul ain the Turkish Defense  Ministry declared victory over the  Kurdish SDF forces for a second time  here on Monday Kurdish fighters have put  up fierce resistance and these are  Syrian soldiers in the town of tel otama  just a few kilometers away after a deal  was made between the SDF and the Syrian  government state media said the army  would confront Turkish aggression the  Turkish president remained defiant we  are not going to enter manbij the real  owners of that area are our Arabic  brothers and they are going to enter  that area our approach to this is that  they are going to enter there and we are  going to make it secure for them the  Syrian Kurds have made deals with  Damascus before especially in the battle  against ISIL but an SDF commander said  they were faced with a difficult choice  this time there is little trust between  the two sides but the SDF quickly  suffered significant losses during  battles with Turkish forces in their  Syrian or rebel allies it's an important  deal because the Kurds and the Assad  regime and Damascus  both have the same enemies they have  turkey as their enemy number one and the  Islamist rebel groups as their enemy  number two this is a long-standing you  know in a sense I wouldn't say  partnership but it's an uneasy  partnership that they've had Damascus  cannot rule Northeast Syria without the  Kurds turkey says this military campaign  is targeting the SD s main Kurdish  fighting force which it says is aligned  with the outlawed Kurdistan Workers  Party or PKK which has been fighting the  Turkish government for decades turkey  says it wants to set up a safe haven for  refugees to return to in northern Syria  but the UN says around half a million  people could be forced from their homes  if the violence doesn't stop US defense  secretary mark Esper says a deal with  the SDF and damascus meant having US  forces stuck between the syrian and  Turkey  armies was untenable the Syrian army has  moved north to potentially confront  Turkish forces at various points close  to the border the SDF hoped that by  teaming up with the Syrian military they  can force Turkish forces to retreat but  at this stage that seems highly unlikely  despite the threat of potential  sanctions from some European countries  and the US president orowan says he has  a plan for northern Syria and no amount  of threats are going to stop him from  achieving his goal  Charles trafford al Jazeera close to the  turkish-syrian border
 

